scenario the receiver's idea of the time drifts away from the device's
describe Two absolute instants compared, which is what a wall clock is for.
describe This is also the detector clock.h protects: a spoofer able to step the
describe clock we measure timeouts against would switch off the detector meant
describe to catch it, so elapsed time is never measured this way.

at 0
  fix 3d
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 11 14
  jam none
  spoof none
  rtime 1700000000 valid
  dtime 1700000002
  expect trust trusted
  expect no-reason clock-disagreement

# Ten minutes apart. One of the two is wrong and this cannot say which.
at 2000
  fix 3d
  pos 5000010 10000010
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 11 14
  jam none
  spoof none
  rtime 1700000602 valid
  dtime 1700000004
  expect reason clock-disagreement
  expect trust degraded

# A receiver that says its own time is not to be trusted is not evidence about
# anything, and must not keep the alarm standing on its own.
at 4000
  fix 3d
  pos 5000020 10000020
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 11 14
  jam none
  spoof none
  rtime 1700000604 invalid
  dtime 1700000006
  expect no-reason clock-disagreement
